/* This is the library of fields that can be referenced from
   a driver with library { use = total_m3 }

   The library speeds up creating drivers for meters with mostly
   standardized values. It also helps normalize the names of the fields.

   For naming fields, there are three types of meters:

   small (low complexity when naming fields)
   medium (medium complexity when naming fields)
   large (high complexity when naming fields industrial meters)

   SMALL / LOW COMPLEXITY NAMING FIELDS

   The small meters (typically household meters) measure consumption
   only for billing.  They might have return flows but mostly for
   failure detection. The have a few flags for warnings and failure
   modes. They might have some historical values.  They only have a
   single primary medium or purpose (ie water or heating or cooling or electricity
   etc eg no combination like heating and cooling)

   For these meters it is implicit that all fields measure consumption, no need to spell it out.
   Since there is only one primary medium there is no need to spell out what is consumed.

   Therefore a field name is short. For a single direction meter with only consumption
   values. Use for example:
   total_m3 (for water/gas consumption volume)
   total_kwh (for energy consumption)
   Sometimes the quantity is repeated in the name, it is obvious that kw is power, but the
   field must have a name, so in these case we use the quantity or something similar.
   power_kw (for the instantaneous power measurement)
   flow_m3h (for the instantaneous flow, but mostlikely it is max over a period)
   The HCA (Heat Cost Allocation) quantity is a number that calculates a relation room temp,
   radiator temp over time. This value does not say how much energy is used, instead it is a
   dimensionless measurement used to share the house costs for heating. Like power we repeat a word
   similar to the quantity in the name.
   allocation_hca (for the instantaneous heat cost allocation value from the radiator)

   The total accumulated at the end of last month is usually called:
   target_m3
   target_kwh
   target_hca

   These are useful for billing since the readout can happen at
   any time during the next month.
   Sometimes even older targets are provided, the even older target value
   will be named: target_h1_m3, target_h2_m3, etc...
   where h stands for history.

   There can be multiple subnits and tariffs suffixed at the end.
   total_tariff1_m3
   total_tariff2_m3
   total_subunit2_tariff1_m3

   Simple heat meters for household consumption often have primary medium used energy
   for total_kwh, but also a secondary medium like water m3 for the water flow used
   to carry the heat, this can still be a simple meter. They have more flags and error states.

   Door/window detectors, temp/hygro meters, etc are all simple meters.
   Having a lot of flags or configuration settings does not necessarily
   mean the meter is medium or large.

   The iperl.xmq driver is an example of a small meter.
   The kamwater.xmq driver has a lot of details, but it is still a single primary medium,
   so the driver (despite its length) is for a small meter.

   MEDIUM / MEDIUM COMPLEXITY NAMING FIELDS

   The medium sized meters can track consumption and production, or they track
   heating and cooling at the same time. I.e. not a single primary medium.

   total_energy_consumption_kwh (Electricity consumed your appliances and heating.)
   total_energy_production_kwh  (Electricity produced solar panels.)
   target_energy_consumption_kwh (Billing.)
   target_energy_production_kwh (Billing.)

   total_cooling_energy_kwh (Cooling energy acquired.)
   total_heating_energy_kwh (Heatin energy acquired.)
   total_cooling_volume_m3

   Example drivers are sharky774.xmq and omipower.xmq (both needs some field renaming)

   LARGE / HIGH COMPLEXITY NAMING FIELDS

   Now we also have different versions of the same quantity of the same medium,
   for example active, reactive, apparent energy totals which
   might also be split over three phase pairs l1,l2,l3.

   total_active_energy_consumption_l1_kwh
   total_net_reactive_energy_kvarh
   total_reactive_energy_consumption_l1_kwh
   total_reactive_energy_capacitive_kvarh
   reactive_power_inductive_kvar

   The amiplus.xmq and iem3000.xmq driver is an example of such a meter.

   There should almost always be a status field (with
   attribute=STATUS) that accumulates all error flags.  If the
   telegram includes a TPL status byte, then those flags (as seen
   below) are automatically included the status field.

   All flags that a driver uses must be declared either in the flags
   here in the library, or in the driver flags entry.

*/
library {
    flags {
        // The following flags are defined in the standard [EN 13757-7:2018 §7.5.6] for the TPL status byte.
        // The error flag is defined in  [EN 13757-7:2018 §7.5.6; EN 13757-3:2018 §10; OMS Vol.2 §8.8].
        flag {
            name = BUSY
            info = 'Meter busy. (tpl sts)'
        }
        flag {
            name = ERROR
            info = 'Meter error; details via error reporting. (tpl sts)'
        }
        flag {
            name = ALARM
            info = 'Abnormal condition/alarm. (tpl sts)'
        }
        flag {
            name = POWER_LOW
            info = 'Power low. (tpl sts)'
        }
        flag {
            name = PERMANENT_ERROR
            info = 'Permanent meter error. (tpl sts)'
        }
        flag {
            name = TEMPORARY_ERROR
            info = 'Temporary meter error. (tpl sts)'
        }
    }
    template(id = total_m3)
    {
        name     = total
        quantity = Volume
        info     = 'The total {media} volume recorded.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Volume
        }
    }
    template(id = total_kwh)
    {
        name     = total
        quantity = Energy
        info     = 'The total {media} energy recorded.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = AnyEnergyVIF
        }
    }
    template(id = target_m3)
    {
        name     = target
        quantity = Volume
        info     = 'The {water} volume recorded at the last billing date.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Volume
            storage_nr       = 1
        }
    }
    template(id = target_kwh)
    {
        name     = target
        quantity = Energy
        info     = 'The {water} energy recorded at the last billing date.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = AnyEnergyVIF
            storage_nr       = 1
        }
    }
    template(id = status)
    {
        name = status
        // Kept working for old C++ drivers that use alias status-tpl-only
        aliases    = status-tpl-only
        quantity   = Flags
        info       = 'Status and error flags.'
        attributes = STATUS,INCLUDE_TPL_STATUS
    }
    template(id = actuality_duration_s)
    {
        name         = actuality_duration
        quantity     = Time
        info         = 'Lapsed time between measurement and transmission.'
        display_unit = s
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ActualityDuration
        }
    }
    template(id = actuality_duration_h)
    {
        name     = actuality_duration
        quantity = Time
        info     = 'Lapsed time between measurement and transmission.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ActualityDuration
        }
    }
    template(id = battery_v)
    {
        name     = battery
        quantity = Voltage
        info     = 'Battery voltage.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Voltage
        }
    }
    template(id = battery_y)
    {
        name         = battery
        quantity     = Time
        info         = 'Remaining battery life in years.'
        display_unit = y
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = RemainingBattery
        }
    }
    template(id = fabrication_no)
    {
        name     = fabrication_no
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Fabrication number.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = FabricationNo
        }
    }
    template(id = enhanced_id)
    {
        name     = enhanced_id
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Enhanced identification number.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = EnhancedIdentification
        }
    }
    template(id = software_version)
    {
        name     = software_version
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Software version.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = SoftwareVersion
        }
    }
    template(id = manufacturer)
    {
        name     = manufacturer
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Meter manufacturer.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Manufacturer
        }
    }
    template(id = model_version)
    {
        name     = model_version
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Meter model version.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ModelVersion
        }
    }
    template(id = firmware_version)
    {
        name     = firmware_version
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Meter firmware version.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = FirmwareVersion
        }
    }
    template(id = parameter_set)
    {
        name     = parameter_set
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Parameter set for this meter.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ParameterSet
        }
    }
    template(id = customer)
    {
        name     = customer
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Customer name.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Customer
        }
    }
    template(id = location)
    {
        name     = location
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Meter installed at this customer location.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Location
        }
    }
    template(id = operating_time_h)
    {
        name     = operating_time
        quantity = Time
        info     = 'How long the meter has been collecting data.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = OperatingTime
        }
    }
    template(id = on_time_h)
    {
        name     = on_time
        quantity = Time
        info     = 'How long the meter has been powered up.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = OnTime
        }
    }
    template(id = on_time_at_error_h)
    {
        name     = on_time_at_error
        quantity = Time
        info     = 'How long the meter has been in an error state while powered up.'
        match {
            measurement_type = AtError
            vif_range        = OnTime
        }
    }
    template(id = meter_date)
    {
        name     = meter_date
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Date when the meter sent the telegram.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Date
        }
    }
    template(id = meter_date_at_error)
    {
        name     = meter_date_at_error
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Date when the meter was in error.'
        match {
            measurement_type = AtError
            vif_range        = Date
        }
    }
    template(id = meter_datetime)
    {
        name     = meter_datetime
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Date and time when the meter sent the telegram.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = DateTime
        }
    }
    template(id = meter_datetime_at_error)
    {
        name     = meter_datetime_at_error
        quantity = Text
        info     = 'Date and time when the meter was in error.'
        match {
            measurement_type = AtError
            vif_range        = DateTime
        }
    }
    template(id = target_date)
    {
        name         = target
        quantity     = PointInTime
        info         = 'The target date. Usually the end of the previous billing period.'
        display_unit = date
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Date
            storage_nr       = 1
        }
    }
    template(id = total_forward_m3)
    {
        name     = total_forward
        quantity = Volume
        info     = 'The total {media} volume flowing forward.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Volume
            add_combinable   = ForwardFlow
        }
    }
    template(id = total_backward_m3)
    {
        name     = total_backward
        quantity = Volume
        info     = 'The total {media} volume flowing backward.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = Volume
            add_combinable   = BackwardFlow
        }
    }
    template(id = flow_temperature_c)
    {
        name     = flow_temperature
        quantity = Temperature
        info     = 'Forward media temperature.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = FlowTemperature
        }
    }
    template(id = external_temperature_c)
    {
        name     = external_temperature
        quantity = Temperature
        info     = 'Temperature outside of meter.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ExternalTemperature
        }
    }
    template(id = return_temperature_c)
    {
        name     = return_temperature
        quantity = Temperature
        info     = 'Return media temperature.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ReturnTemperature
        }
    }
    template(id = flow_return_temperature_difference_c)
    {
        name     = flow_return_temperature_difference
        quantity = Temperature
        info     = 'The difference between flow and return media temperatures.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = TemperatureDifference
        }
    }
    template(id = volume_flow_m3h)
    {
        name     = volume_flow
        quantity = Flow
        info     = 'Media volume flow.'
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = VolumeFlow
        }
    }
    template(id = access_counter)
    {
        name           = access
        quantity       = Dimensionless
        info           = 'Meter access counter.'
        vif_scaling    = None
        dif_signedness = Unsigned
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = AccessNumber
        }
    }
    template(id = rssi_dbm)
    {
        name           = rssi
        quantity       = Power
        display_unit   = dbm
        info           = 'The RSSI reception level reported by the gateway.'
        vif_scaling    = None
        dif_signedness = Signed
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = ReceptionLevel
        }
    }
    template(id = consumption_hca)
    {
        name     = consumption
        quantity = HCA
        info     = 'The current heat cost allocation for this meter.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = HeatCostAllocation
        }
    }
    template(id = target_hca)
    {
        name     = target
        quantity = HCA
        info     = 'The heat cost allocation recorded by this meter at the target date.'
        change   = Increasing
        match {
            measurement_type = Instantaneous
            vif_range        = HeatCostAllocation
            storage_nr       = 1
        }
    }
}
